# Cloudflare Pages redirects. (Vercel, the earlier host, ignores this file.)
#
# HOW CLOUDFLARE READS THIS FILE — checked on 2026-10-17 against workers-sdk's redirect parser and
# the Pages asset server; parseRedirects() in src/lib/engines/publication.mjs reads it the same way
# and src/lib/engines/publication.test.ts holds the file to these three rules:
#
#   1. Only a rule ABOVE the first splat (*) or placeholder (:name) counts as static (2,000
#      allowed). Every rule after the first pattern counts against the 100 dynamic rules, exact or
#      not, and once those are spent the rest of the file is skipped. Until 2026-10-17 this file's
#      second line was a splat, so 64 of its 65 rules were already dynamic. Hence two parts: every
#      exact path in PART 1, every pattern in PART 2.
#   2. At request time every exact rule is looked up before any pattern; the patterns are tried in
#      order and the first match wins — a specific pattern stands above a general one.
#   3. A redirect fires before Pages looks for a file. A rule that matches a published file takes
#      that file off the site.
#
# Both slash forms are listed for an exact path where both were ever served: Pages matches the
# path exactly, so `/lab` does not catch `/lab/`.

